=== Auto-sell Zodiacs ===

Unlocked by beating Hard Trial 3 for reaching Unity without performing a Supernova

Allows you to automatically sell unwanted zodiacs based on: Sign, Rarity, Quality and Level.

Optional for cases when you're getting lots of zodiacs and need to get rid of some. Be very careful with this so as to not sell the zodiacs you need!

This is an automation that if you get or have any zodiacs that meet all 5 specified req, it will be sold into the shop for Astrodust.

Reqs

1 sign - you must specify the signs that you want the automation to sell (you can select multiple)

2 Rarity - you much select every rarity that you want the automation to sell (you can select multiple)

3 Quality - you must input the range that you want any zodiacs to be for it to sell, so if you want it to sell any zodiac from qual 1 to qual 100 you need to put in min 1 and max 100, using this example any zodiacs with their quality being 1-100 will be sold (assuming all other checks are also correct)

4 Level - you must input the range of levels that you want to sell, so if you want it to sell any zodiacs from lv 1-100 you must input 1 in min and 100 in max, this will sell any lv1-100 zodiacs any 101 or higher will not be sold

5 Inventory - for any zodiacs to be eligible to be sold they must be in your inventory, if you have a zodiac and it meets all other reqs for being sold, but you have it equipped on one of your planets it will not be sold, the automation will only check for zodiacs in your inventory

ALL 5 REQS MUST BE MET TO BE SOLD BY YOUR AUTOMATION

=== Auto Unity ===

Unlocked by beating Medium Trial 4 for reaching Eternity by performing Infinity a maximum of 2 times.

Allows you to automatically unite after reaching required EP, Zodiac lvl, Attack lvl and Gold gain upon unity. Chooses a zodiac based on Rarity, Sign, Stat, Element and Season, priority levels can be assigned to these requirements.

Can be useful for farming better quality zodiacs, astrodust, gold, etc.

When configuring auto unite, the priority is lowest to highest so 0>1>2>3>4>5, also as of v.1.1004, the game sees all Immortal and Immortal+ zodiacs as just Immortal, so your secondary priority is also very important to set, if you want max rarity.

