== Macros ==
Macros allow you to execute a specific order of actions without any need for your input. Initially you have a limit of 3 macros (more can be bought with souls) and 30 blocks (same applies) within every macro. Some blocks need to bought with souls before they can be used.

Additionally every macro can have 3 extra settings applied: 

Loop mode, making it loop back when completed.

Startup Execution, executing the macro upon entering the game.

Logs, allows you to view the logs of the macro. They show every step of the macro and can help in debugging.

=== Macro blocks ===
There are 30* macro blocks you can use, categorized by their type of action, see the table for details. (Blocks denoted with an * are either bought with souls or not in the game yet.)

''For macro blocks explanations, see [[Macro Builder#Blockdex|Blockdex]].''

Some useful Macros throughout the game are:

* IC macro
* EC macro
* Unity farm macro
* Astrodust farm macro
* Zodiac quality farm macro
* Attacks grind macro
''For macro templates, see [[Macro Templates]].''

The 30 macro block maximum is pretty limiting, buying the "Go to macro" block is recommended, especially after getting to the mid to late stages of unity.

The other buyable blocks are not all that useful in comparison.

